	:hasThumbnail :Hugo_Filipe_Silva_Ribeiro_pdf_jpg .

:204222753 a :Record ;
	:title "HandyTAT a text-alignment toolkit" ;
	:type "masterThesis" ;
	:description "This dissertation introduces HandyTAT, a versatile toolkit designed to streamline text alignment processes\ncritical to numerous natural language processing (NLP) tasks, such as machine translation, multilingual\ndata analysis, and content localization. Despite the importance of text alignment, existing tools are often\nchallenging to install, configure, and operate effectively, requiring significant technical expertise that\nlimits accessibility for many users. HandyTAT directly addresses these obstacles by offering a suite of\nintegrated tools, including HandyAlign and HandySubl, which provide both command-line and graphical\nuser interfaces tailored for enhanced usability and precision.\nHandyAlign is a command-line alignment tool optimized to simplify sentence and word alignment tasks,\ndelivering fast alignment results in a user-friendly manner. It includes automated preprocessing functions\nthat reduce the need for manual text preparation, thus accelerating the alignment workflow. Furthermore,\nit includes an alignment graph visualization tool and multiple file formats support. HandySubl, on the other\nhand, is an advanced text editor extension based on Sublime Text, designed specifically for aligned text\nmanipulation. With features like synchronized editing, intuitive navigation, and TMX (Translation Memory\neXchange) format compatibility, HandySubl provides an accessible editing environment where users can\nvisualize, adjust, and refine alignment results.\nThe toolkit’s development incorporates contemporary programming methodologies, ensuring compatibility\nwith various alignment formats while allowing for continued customization and updates." ;
	:language "eng" ;
	:rights "openAccess" ;
	:createdBy :João_Esteves_Gonçalves ;
	:contributionBy :J_J_Almeida ;
	:hasSubject :Toolkit, :Text_alignment, :NLP_toolkit, :HandyTAT, :HandyAlign, :HandySubl, :Sentence_alignment, :Word_alignment, :Alinhamento_de_textos, :Ferramenta_PLN, :Alinhamento_de_frases, :Alinhamento_de_palavras ;
	:issuedDate "2025-02-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
