	:hasThumbnail :Joao_Vieira_da_Silva_Fernandes_pdf_jpg .

:203992970 a :Record ;
	:title "Anomaly detection as a quality control tool in an industrial context" ;
	:type "masterThesis" ;
	:description "This thesis reports on the development of an automated anomaly detection (AD) systemfor industrial\nquality control (QC), addressing inefficiencies of manual inspections and current practices. Leveraging\nmachine learning and computer vision techniques, this work optimizes QC using AD algorithms.\nThe research includes a review of AD techniques, algorithm development, hyperparameter optimization,\nperformance evaluation, real-time implementation, and API backend creation. Central to this\nwork is a framework built on an autoencoder (AE) architecture, optimized with a custom objective\nfunction that leverages data augmentation techniques to be trained using only defect-free images.\nDesigned as a plug-and-play solution, it can be deployed across various production lines via API calls.\nThis study assessed fourmethodologies, each building upon the one before, except for the variational\napproach, which showed no improvements. The best strategy involved a refined hyperparameter optimization\ncoupled with advanced data augmentation techniques. The overall results were primarily\nattributed to the developed post-processing techniques and the use of the BCE metric for evaluation.\nIn academic evaluations on theMetal Nut subset of the MVTec AD dataset, thiswork surpassedSOTA in\nthe MSE AE regime, achieving an AUC of 0.87 and an IoU of 0.37, outperforming handcrafted methods\nin the literature by ≈ 1.2% and ≈ 42.3%, respectively. Although only slightly outperformed in AUC\nby the top SOTA method, which achieved 0.89, the methodology still delivered highly competitive\nresults. In collaboration with industrial partners, the system successfully detected anomalous parts\nusing a real-world dataset.\nThe results validate the novel methodology and showcases the potential of data-augmented NOKs as\nan alternative to real-world defects. Aligned with Industry 4.0 objectives, this work contributes to the\nadvancement of smarter, data-driven manufacturing processes, facilitating the development of more\nautomated quality control systems, reducing industrywaste, and improving market competitiveness." ;
	:language "eng" ;
	:rights "openAccess" ;
	:createdBy :Miguel_Caçador_Peixoto ;
	:contributionBy :Nuno_Filipe_Castro ;
	:hasSubject :Anomaly_Detection, :Quality_Control, :Computer_Vision, :Autoencoders, :Waste_Reduction, :Machine_Learning, :Real_Time_Implementation, :HyperparameterOptimization, :Semi_Supervised_Learning, :Defective_Products, :Machine_Learning_Backend, :Deteção_de_Anomalias, :Controlo_de_Qualidade, :Visão_Computacional, :Redução_de_Desperdício, :AprendizagemAutomática, :ImplementaçãoemTempoReal, :Otimização_de_Hiperparâmetros, :AprendizagemSemi_Supervisionada, :Produtos_Defeituosos, :Backendde_Aprendizagem_Automática ;
