:204230195 a :Record ;
	:title "Update processing in polystores" ;
	:type "masterThesis" ;
	:description "The proposed dissertation addresses polyglot persistence, the concept of using different data stores together\nto address different aspects of a processing application. Although there are numerous approaches\nto optimize analytical polyglot workloads, managing updates remains a critical challenge. This challenge\narises from the inherent diversity of data models in native stores, the complexity of leveraging their full\npotential, and the difficulty of reconciling robustness, and efficiency.\nThis work is motivated by real-world scenarios in which organizations need to integrate and operate\non data distributed across different companies, each using distinct and specialized data storage technologies.\nIn such cases, enabling seamless updates across heterogeneous systems is crucial to maintain\nconsistency, enabling collaboration, and supporting evolving business needs.\nWe address this challenge with an update processing model based on relational updatable views.\nThis allows us to take full advantage of native query capabilities while simplifying the mapping for update\noperations. We verify the feasibility of the proposal by applying it to MongoDB and Unicage mainly, with\nthe implementation of the required query optimization functionality." ;
	:language "eng" ;
	:rights "openAccess" ;
	:createdBy :Luís_Manuel_Peixoto_Silva ;
	:contributionBy :José_Pereira ;
	:hasSubject :Query_translation, :Query_optimization, :Polyglot, :Transaction_isolation, :Optimização_de_consultas, :Tradução_de_consultas, :Poliglota, :Isolamento_de_transação ;
	:issuedDate "2025-07-14T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
	:accessionedDate "2026-03-16T12:29:43Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
	:submittedDate "2025-04-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
